                <pb facs="0519" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No 6775/572.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Heimke to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Guatemala
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-09-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Yesterday afternoon the President of Guatemala, with the assistance of cabinet
                    members, supreme court, army officers, diplomatic corps and civic bodies,
                    officially inaugurated the International Bureau of Central American Republics,
                    in impressive ceremony and amid greatest enthusiasm.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Heimke.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
